  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Polyphillin C and the CD70 antigen, as it is indirectly linked through multiple pathways. Polyphillin C is predicted to target WiDr, a cell line that is itself a target of Tenuiphenone B, which in turn targets the CD70 antigen. Additionally, Polyphillin C is predicted to target DMS-79, a cell line that is also a target of another compound, which ultimately targets the CD70 antigen. These findings collectively indicate that Polyphillin C may exert its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of the CD70 antigen. The scores from the different paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, though the strength of the evidence varies across the pathways. The indirect nature of the relationships implies that the observed effects may be mediated through intermediate targets, highlighting the complexity of the molecular mechanisms involved.",
